    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: First-Time Visitors Rental Paperwork Questions</h1>
    <p>The paperwork conversation is the least glamorous part of a first motorbike rental and the part that protects the whole trip. Five calm minutes of questions before riding prevent the disputes, surprises and ambiguities that otherwise surface at the worst moments: at a checkpoint, at a scratch, or at the return counter on departure day. This guide lists the questions first-time visitors should actually ask, in the order worth asking them, with the standing rule that our specific terms are always agreed directly with us rather than assumed from any article.</p>
    <p>This page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> series for first-time visitors, focused strictly on the paperwork conversation. The verified prices for every machine are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost hub</a>, the general rental questions are collected on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the deposit-side detail has its own <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/motorbike-rental-deposit-hanoi/">deposit guide</a> in this cluster.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the questions matter more than the paper</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Rental period, rates and what the price includes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Deposits: ask the shape, not just the amount</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Condition, damage and the photo record</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Helmets, accessories and what else is provided</a></li>
